// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A14. AGG() in a correlated scalar subquery in WHERE.
// Question: In each department, how many employees earn more than the average
//   of their own department?
// The subquery reads the department of the outer row. It stays where it is,
// with its measure written out, because blocks in front of the query could
// not read the outer row.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// KQL: agg() in a scalar sub-query of the FILTER that reads an alias of the outer query.
FIND emp e
FILTER e.sal > (FIND emp x FILTER x.deptno = e.deptno FETCH agg(x.avg_sal))
FETCH e.deptno ASC, agg(e.emp_count) empcount
